{"agent_id":"79Ig","agent_seq":112,"timestamp":"2026-07-22T17:38:45.918764Z","event":{"type":"CommentAdded","issue_uuid":"7d222949-0302-4dc4-9859-143cf7da11fb","comment_uuid":"7b3cace9-64b2-4af6-95b2-7f27e9a10087","author":"79Ig","content":"Four pending operator/SO decisions, batched for one ratification pass. Each has full context on its source issue; this issue is the single home now that #77/#78 are closed with their code shipped.\n\nD1 — VERIFY DEFAULT when config.yaml is absent (#77 residual, consumer preference: route-only). Current: walk-all (**/*.md). Route-only is closed-world-correct (Thermite spec-routes.toml precedent) and retires the unrouted-third-party-file class entirely, but is a behavior change for config-less trees (verify would validate nothing until globs are declared — arguably correct: no jurisdiction declared, nothing governed). NOTE: init seeds config.yaml with **/*.md, so any init'd tree has explicit globs; the default only bites non-init'd trees.\n\nD2 — LOUDNESS for routed-but-frontmatterless files (#78 ask b). A file matching a governed glob (or a configured must-have-frontmatter glob) that parses to Ok(None) currently passes silently — indistinguishable from validated-clean. Proposal: a W-code in the config/governance range (W0040-99) e.g. MDATRON-W0040 'governed-file-has-no-frontmatter', opt-in via config to avoid blanket noise on prose-only md. Needs DESIGN language.\n\nD3 — NUMERIC-CLAIMS family scope (#79). First body-prose primitive vs the deliberately-narrowed DSL; DESIGN gates body-content extraction behind a falsifiability run at the 80% bar (DESIGN L85), so ratifying scope likely also schedules a falsifiability increment (#47 synergy). Conservative first cut: configured field references only; vsdd contributes 3 historical drift fixtures.\n\nD4 — COMPACT per-finding SIZE-LIMIT number (#44, deferred from phase 1b alongside the mutation floor). A contract limit, not a band from actuals (DESIGN L29). Strawman for ratification: 512 bytes per finding in compact form (fits code+summary+location+one marked quoted line for typical findings; ~an order of magnitude under typical hook context budgets); truncation at line boundary + elision marker per DESIGN L30. The mutation-testing kill-ratio floor (also phase-1b-deferred) could ride the same ruling if desired.\n\nRulings can be dropped as comments here; each then routes to its build lane (D1/D2 small; D3 = #45 design pass; D4 unblocks #44 compact-verify).","created_at":"2026-07-22T17:38:45.904852Z","kind":"plan","signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAARY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWNvbW1lbnQAAAAAAAAABnNoYTUxMgAAAFMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAABA2g1QkopZ+inAc8ntHT6HenBjXp8XQ3BbJwnDf6PX3F6mfhur5iinsjrdPCeMf6yQ3gHRfT0Ai3yrO1WN/FPpAA=="},"signed_by":"SHA256:u0VtJEsnHrvNPG5QQKKfDO+Rro/KT/xZqEvahzZTqEA","signature":"U1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgOk7MLoVvSEPAWM9VkHKFnHq8O1iEkPSfqY7zLc4I28oAAAAPY3Jvc3NsaW5rLWV2ZW50AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAj05EG3d1eEWC+Zvs7PsnCK8ObwrC6yoZrocC7xWCJhnq1KORtJHsFU3f2O4j50xOMacqyFdfRdbsNkQJieAgA="}
